From d8a18205f5d4ffef79aeb0554c9f0ff8a3471f49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minhmc2007 <quangminh21072010@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:00:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] libsndfile: name the library module libsndfile12

error: external/pulseaudio/src/Android.bp:82:1: "libpulse" depends on
undefined module "libsndfile12".

Upstream 22.2 pairs the pulseaudio fork at lineage-20 with the libsndfile
fork at lineage-20, but the two disagree. pulseaudio was written against
AOSP's external/libsndfile, which names the soname-versioned module
libsndfile12; the fork kept the older AOSP name libsndfile_linux. LineageOS
22.2 has no external/libsndfile of its own, so nothing else supplies the
name.

Nothing outside this Android.bp references libsndfile_linux. The remaining
libsndfile hits in the tree are host test targets that are not part of a
phone build. Renaming is enough; pulseaudio reaches the headers through
include_dirs, not through the module.
---
 Android.bp | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 6156f05..ac53ffe 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -9,14 +9,14 @@ license {
 }
 
 cc_defaults {
-    name: "libsndfile_linux_defaults",
+    name: "libsndfile12_defaults",
     c_std: "gnu99",
     cflags: ["-Wall"],
 }
 
 cc_library_shared {
-    name: "libsndfile_linux",
-    defaults: ["libsndfile_linux_defaults"],
+    name: "libsndfile12",
+    defaults: ["libsndfile12_defaults"],
     vendor: true,
 
     srcs: [
